# A session finishes while the user is in another tab, so its tab carries the unread
# mark and the phone gets the result. The user answers from the phone. That answer is
# proof the result was read, so the mark goes at once, before Copilot has even picked
# the reply up; the stub never starts a turn on plain text, so nothing else could clear it.

size 110x30
arg --mux
fake_telegram private
session existing-app Existing app session
session other-app Other session

# Two tabs: whichever row is first opens first, then the other.
wait_for Other session
press enter
wait_for Fake Copilot is idling
press ctrl+b d
wait_for Other session
press down
press enter
wait_for --resume=00000002-0000-4000-8000-000000000002

# A turn in the previous tab, watched from this one, so its end is unread there.
press ctrl+b p
wait_for --resume=00000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
type e2e:work 3000 Done thinking about it.
press enter
press ctrl+b n
telegram_wait Done thinking about it.
wait_for ●
dump 01-unread-tab

# Answering from the phone reads it: the mark is gone while the other tab stays focused.
telegram_say Thanks, carry on
telegram_wait reaction on
wait_gone ●
dump 02-read-from-phone
